what is EBS
    Amazon EBS (Elastic Block Store) is a block storage service in AWS used to provide persistent storage for EC2 instances.
        1) here the dat will maintain in multiple blocks
        2) connot acces from the multiple server can mount to single server
        3) better for updating the data because while updating that only one block will be updated
    EBS = Hard disk for EC2
        Attached to EC2 instance
        Stores OS, applications, and data
        Data is not lost even if instance stops
    types:
        gp3/gp2 → General purpose
        io1/io2 → High performance
        magnetic 
    root volume
    ------------
        by default a volume is Attached to the ec2 which we call it as root volume it  is helpful for  the booting the os
        and we can attach more than 1 ebs to an ec2 which is mutli ebs attach
    
for list out how many ebs volumes connected  to know it use below cmd
    cmd : lsblk
to know the ebs connected to which path use below cmd
    cmd: df -h

types of EBS
------------
    general purpose (gp2)
    general purpose (gp3)
    privisioned IOPs (IO1)
    privisioned IOPs (IO2)
    cold HDD 
    throughput optimized HDD
    magnetic standard

🔹 1) General Purpose SSD
    ✅ gp2
    Balanced price & performance
    Older generation
    ✅ gp3 (Recommended)
    Better performance than gp2
    Lower cost 💰
    You can configure IOPS & throughput separately

    👉 🔥 Most commonly used

🔹 2) Provisioned IOPS SSD
    ✅ io1
    High performance SSD
    Used for critical applications
    ✅ io2
    Higher durability & performance than io1
    Used for mission-critical databases

    👉 Example:

    Banking systems
High-end databases
🔹 3) HDD (Hard Disk Drives)
    ✅ st1 (Throughput Optimized HDD)
    Good for large data workloads
    High throughput

    👉 Use cases:

    Big data
    Logs processing
    ✅ sc1 (Cold HDD)
    Lowest cost 💰
Used for infrequently accessed data
🔹 4) Magnetic (Standard)
    ✅ Standard (Magnetic)
    Old generation
    Low performance
    Rarely used now ❌